[2026-01-05 21:15:33] {"conversation_id":"1d95a7c0-f530-43e4-90c1-fef078437daa","generation_id":"e353d596-3fcc-4cb0-8eb4-14bcc0d8b92b","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/.cursor/plans/cursor_mental_models_dictionary_7b20c779.plan.md","edits":[{"old_string":"---\nname: Cursor Mental Models Dictionary\noverview: Build a static single-page demo website that displays mental models for Cursor as an interactive card grid with search and modal detail views, using plain HTML/CSS/vanilla JS with data loaded from JSON.\ntodos: []\n---\n\n# Cursor Mental Models Dictionary - Implementation Plan\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nA static single-page application that dynamically loads mental model data from JSON and renders an interactive card grid with search and modal detail views.\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nmental-models.json → app.js (fetch) → renderCards() → DOM\n                                    → filterCards() → renderCards()\n                                    → openModal() → renderModal()\n```\n\n### File Responsibilities\n\n- **`index.html`**: Base HTML structure with semantic elements (header, search input, cards container, modal overlay)\n- **`styles.css`**: Complete styling system (layout, cards, modal, colors, typography)\n- **`app.js`**: All JavaScript logic (data loading, rendering, search filtering, modal management)\n- **`data/mental-models.json`**: Single source of truth for all mental model content\n- **`README.md`**: Project documentation explaining purpose and usage\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### HTML Structure (`index.html`)\n\n- Semantic HTML5 structure\n- Header section with title and subtitle\n- Search input with placeholder text\n- Grid container for cards (initially empty, populated by JS)\n- Modal overlay (hidden by default) with:\n  - Close button\n  - Title\n  - Detailed explanation list\n  - Related features section\n  - Documentation links section\n\n### CSS Architecture (`styles.css`)\n\n- CSS custom properties for colors (design system)\n- Base typography and reset styles\n- Header and search bar layout\n- Responsive grid layout for cards (CSS Grid)\n- Card styling (white background, rounded corners, shadow, hover effects)\n- Feature tag styling (light blue background)\n- Modal overlay (full-screen backdrop, centered content box)\n- Modal content layout (scrollable if needed)\n- Responsive breakpoints for mobile/tablet\n\n### JavaScript Logic (`app.js`)\n\n**State Management:**\n\n- `mentalModels` array (loaded from JSON)\n- `filteredModels` array (search results)\n- `currentModalId` (string | null)\n\n**Core Functions:**\n\n- `loadData()`: Fetch JSON, parse, store in `mentalModels`, call `renderCards()`\n- `renderCards()`: Clear container, iterate `filteredModels`, create card DOM elements, attach click handlers\n- `filterCards(searchTerm)`: Case-insensitive filter on title/description, update `filteredModels`, call `renderCards()`\n- `openModal(modelId)`: Find model by ID, render modal content, show modal overlay\n- `closeModal()`: Hide modal overlay, clear `currentModalId`\n- `init()`: Set up search input listener, attach modal close handlers, call `loadData()`\n\n**Event Handlers:**\n\n- Search input: `input` event → `filterCards()`\n- Card click: `click` event → `openModal()`\n- Modal close: Click overlay or close button → `closeModal()`\n- Escape key: `keydown` event → `closeModal()`\n\n### JSON Schema (`data/mental-models.json`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mentalModels\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"planner\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Planner\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps break down complex tasks into actionable steps.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Analyzes requirements and creates structured plans\",\n        \"Identifies dependencies and order of operations\",\n        \"Produces TODO lists with clear, actionable items\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Planning\", \"Task Breakdown\", \"Dependency Analysis\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Planning Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Design System Implementation\n\n- Background: `#f5f5f5`\n- Cards: `white` with `border-radius: 8px`, `box-shadow`\n- Primary text: `#222` / `#333`\n- Secondary text: `#666`\n- Accent color: `#4f8cff`\n- Feature tags: Background `#e3f0ff`, text `#1e5fcc`\n- System fonts: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif`\n- Spacing: Generous padding/margins (16px, 24px, 32px scale)\n\n## Interaction Flow\n\n1. **Page Load**: `init()` → `loadData()` → fetch JSON → `renderCards()` → display all cards\n2. **Search**: User types → `filterCards()` → update `filteredModels` → `renderCards()` → update display\n3. **Card Click**: User clicks card → `openModal(modelId)` → render modal content → show overlay\n4. **Close Modal**: User clicks overlay/close/Escape → `closeModal()` → hide overlay\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n- No external dependencies (use native `fetch` API)\n- No build step (direct file references)\n- No inline styles (all CSS in `styles.css`)\n- No hardcoded content (all content from JSON)\n- Progressive enhancement (works without JS, but shows message) ","new_string":"---\nname: Cursor Mental Models Dictionary\noverview: Build a static single-page demo website that displays mental models for Cursor as an interactive card grid with search and modal detail views, using plain HTML/CSS/vanilla JS with data loaded from JSON.\ntodos: []\n---\n\n# Cursor Mental Models Dictionary - Implementation Plan\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nA static single-page application that dynamically loads mental model data from JSON and renders an interactive card grid with search and modal detail views.\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nmental-models.json → app.js (fetch) → renderCards() → DOM\n                                    → filterCards() → renderCards()\n                                    → openModal() → renderModal()\n```\n\n### File Responsibilities\n\n- **`index.html`**: Base HTML structure with semantic elements (header, search input, cards container, modal overlay)\n- **`styles.css`**: Complete styling system (layout, cards, modal, colors, typography)\n- **`app.js`**: All JavaScript logic (data loading, rendering, search filtering, modal management)\n- **`data/mental-models.json`**: Single source of truth for all mental model content\n- **`README.md`**: Project documentation explaining purpose and usage\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### HTML Structure (`index.html`)\n\n- Semantic HTML5 structure\n- Header section with title and subtitle\n- Search input with placeholder text\n- Grid container for cards (initially empty, populated by JS)\n- Modal overlay (hidden by default) with:\n  - Close button\n  - Title\n  - Detailed explanation list\n  - Related features section\n  - Documentation links section\n\n### CSS Architecture (`styles.css`)\n\n- CSS custom properties for colors (design system)\n- Base typography and reset styles\n- Header and search bar layout\n- Responsive grid layout for cards (CSS Grid)\n- Card styling (white background, rounded corners, shadow, hover effects)\n- Feature tag styling (light blue background)\n- Modal overlay (full-screen backdrop, centered content box)\n- Modal content layout (scrollable if needed)\n- Responsive breakpoints for mobile/tablet\n\n### JavaScript Logic (`app.js`)\n\n**State Management:**\n\n- `mentalModels` array (loaded from JSON)\n- `filteredModels` array (search results)\n- `currentModalId` (string | null)\n\n**Core Functions:**\n\n- `loadData()`: Fetch JSON, parse, store in `mentalModels`, call `renderCards()`\n- `renderCards()`: Clear container, iterate `filteredModels`, create card DOM elements, attach click handlers\n- `filterCards(searchTerm)`: Case-insensitive filter on title/description, update `filteredModels`, call `renderCards()`\n- `openModal(modelId)`: Find model by ID, render modal content, show modal overlay\n- `closeModal()`: Hide modal overlay, clear `currentModalId`\n- `init()`: Set up search input listener, attach modal close handlers, call `loadData()`\n\n**Event Handlers:**\n\n- Search input: `input` event → `filterCards()`\n- Card click: `click` event → `openModal()`\n- Modal close: Click overlay or close button → `closeModal()`\n- Escape key: `keydown` event → `closeModal()`\n\n### JSON Schema (`data/mental-models.json`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mentalModels\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"planner\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Planner\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps break down complex tasks into actionable steps.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Analyzes requirements and creates structured plans\",\n        \"Identifies dependencies and order of operations\",\n        \"Produces TODO lists with clear, actionable items\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Planning\", \"Task Breakdown\", \"Dependency Analysis\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Planning Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Design System Implementation\n\n- Background: `#f5f5f5`\n- Cards: `white` with `border-radius: 8px`, `box-shadow`\n- Primary text: `#222` / `#333`\n- Secondary text: `#666`\n- Accent color: `#4f8cff`\n- Feature tags: Background `#e3f0ff`, text `#1e5fcc`\n- System fonts: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif`\n- Spacing: Generous padding/margins (16px, 24px, 32px scale)\n\n## Interaction Flow\n\n1. **Page Load**: `init()` → `loadData()` → fetch JSON → `renderCards()` → display all cards\n2. **Search**: User types → `filterCards()` → update `filteredModels` → `renderCards()` → update display\n3. **Card Click**: User clicks card → `openModal(modelId)` → render modal content → show overlay\n4. **Close Modal**: User clicks overlay/close/Escape → `closeModal()` → hide overlay\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n- No external dependencies (use native `fetch` API)\n- No build step (direct file references)\n- No inline styles (all CSS in `styles.css`)\n- No hardcoded content (all content from JSON)\n- Progressive enhancement (works without JS, but shows message)\n\n## TODO List\n\n1. Create directory structure: `data/` folder\n2. Create `data/mental-models.json` with initial mental model entries (5-6 examples)\n3. Create `index.html` skeleton with semantic structure (header, search input, cards container, modal)\n4. Link `styles.css` and `app.js` in `index.html`\n5. Create `styles.css` with CSS custom properties for design system colors\n6. Implement base typography and reset styles in `styles.css`\n7. Style header and search bar layout in `styles.css`\n8. Implement responsive CSS Grid layout for cards container in `styles.css`\n9. Style card components (white background, rounded corners, shadow, hover) in `styles.css`\n10. Style feature tags (light blue background, darker blue text) in `styles.css`\n11. Implement modal overlay styling (full-screen backdrop, centered content) in `styles.css`\n12. Add responsive breakpoints for mobile/tablet in `styles.css`\n13. Create `app.js` with state variables (`mentalModels`, `filteredModels`, `currentModalId`)\n14. Implement `loadData()` function to fetch and parse JSON in `app.js`\n15. Implement `renderCards()` function to dynamically create card DOM elements in `app.js`\n16. Implement `filterCards(searchTerm)` function with case-insensitive search in `app.js`\n17. Implement `openModal(modelId)` function to render and show modal content in `app.js`\n18. Implement `closeModal()` function to hide modal overlay in `app.js`\n19. Implement `init()` function to set up event listeners and initialize app in `app.js`\n20. Add search input event listener in `app.js`\n21. Add card click handlers in `app.js`\n22. Add modal close handlers (overlay click, close button, Escape key) in `app.js`\n23. Create `README.md` with project overview, purpose, and local usage instructions\n24. Test locally by opening `index.html` in browser\n25. Verify all interactions: search filtering, card clicks, modal display, modal closing "}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
