[2026-01-05 21:18:25] {"conversation_id":"1d95a7c0-f530-43e4-90c1-fef078437daa","generation_id":"4726535c-094f-41d8-ad61-7a2bb9b6b908","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/data/mental-models.json","edits":[{"old_string":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"planner\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Planner\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Think of Cursor as a strategic planner that helps break down complex tasks into manageable steps and creates structured roadmaps for your projects.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor can analyze your project requirements and suggest a step-by-step implementation plan\",\n      \"It helps you think through edge cases and potential issues before you start coding\",\n      \"You can ask Cursor to create task breakdowns, timelines, and architectural decisions\",\n      \"It acts like a project manager that understands both technical constraints and business goals\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Task Breakdown\",\n      \"Architecture Planning\",\n      \"Step-by-step Guidance\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - Planning\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"pair-programmer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Pair Programmer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor works alongside you like a collaborative coding partner, helping you write code, debug issues, and explore solutions together in real-time.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor understands the context of your current file and entire codebase\",\n      \"It can suggest code completions that match your coding style and patterns\",\n      \"You can have back-and-forth conversations about implementation approaches\",\n      \"It helps you think through problems by asking clarifying questions and offering alternatives\",\n      \"Like a good pair programmer, it catches potential bugs and suggests improvements\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Code Completions\",\n      \"Context-Aware Suggestions\",\n      \"Interactive Chat\",\n      \"Code Review\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - Pair Programming\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"code-reviewer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Code Reviewer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor acts as an experienced code reviewer, examining your code for bugs, style issues, performance problems, and suggesting improvements.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor can review your code for common bugs, security issues, and anti-patterns\",\n      \"It suggests improvements for readability, maintainability, and performance\",\n      \"It explains why certain changes are recommended, helping you learn best practices\",\n      \"You can ask Cursor to review specific functions, files, or entire pull requests\",\n      \"It provides constructive feedback that helps you write better code over time\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Bug Detection\",\n      \"Code Quality Analysis\",\n      \"Performance Suggestions\",\n      \"Security Review\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - Code Review\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"ci-fixer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a CI Fixer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"When your CI pipeline fails, Cursor helps you understand the errors, fix the issues, and get your builds passing again quickly.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor can read and understand CI error messages, stack traces, and test failures\",\n      \"It helps you identify the root cause of build failures and suggests fixes\",\n      \"You can paste CI logs and Cursor will help debug the specific issues\",\n      \"It understands different CI systems and can help with configuration issues\",\n      \"Cursor can help you write better tests to prevent future CI failures\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Error Analysis\",\n      \"Test Fixes\",\n      \"CI Configuration\",\n      \"Build Debugging\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - CI/CD\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"knowledge-retriever\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor acts as a smart knowledge base that can search through your codebase, documentation, and code history to find relevant information and answer questions.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor can search across your entire codebase to find where specific functionality is implemented\",\n      \"It helps you understand how different parts of your codebase connect and interact\",\n      \"You can ask questions about your codebase and get answers based on actual code\",\n      \"It can help you discover existing patterns, utilities, and conventions in your project\",\n      \"Cursor remembers context from previous conversations and code you've worked on\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Codebase Search\",\n      \"Documentation Lookup\",\n      \"Pattern Discovery\",\n      \"Context Memory\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - Knowledge Base\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"teacher\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Teacher\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor acts as an educational mentor that explains coding concepts, answers questions, and helps you learn best practices while you work.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor can explain complex code patterns, algorithms, and programming concepts in simple terms\",\n      \"It answers your questions about how things work and why certain approaches are used\",\n      \"When reviewing your code, Cursor explains the reasoning behind suggestions, helping you learn\",\n      \"It can break down unfamiliar codebases and teach you about new frameworks or libraries\",\n      \"Cursor helps you understand not just what to do, but why certain solutions are better than others\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Cursor Chat\",\n      \"AI Review\",\n      \"Code Explanations\",\n      \"Context-Aware Suggestions\",\n      \"Long Context Chat\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - Chat\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/chat/overview\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Docs - AI Review\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/advanced/ai-review\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n","new_string":"{\n  \"mentalModels\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"planner\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Planner\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps break down complex tasks into actionable steps.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Analyzes requirements and creates structured plans\",\n        \"Identifies dependencies and order of operations\",\n        \"Produces TODO lists with clear, actionable items\",\n        \"Considers edge cases and potential pitfalls\",\n        \"Suggests implementation phases and milestones\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Planning\", \"Task Breakdown\", \"Dependency Analysis\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Planning Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pair-programmer\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Pair Programmer\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor collaborates with you in real-time, suggesting code as you type.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Provides context-aware code suggestions\",\n        \"Understands your coding style and patterns\",\n        \"Offers alternative implementations\",\n        \"Helps debug issues as they arise\",\n        \"Explains code decisions and trade-offs\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Code Suggestions\", \"Real-time Collaboration\", \"Code Explanation\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Pair Programming Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"code-reviewer\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Code Reviewer\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor reviews your code for bugs, style issues, and improvements.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Identifies potential bugs and security issues\",\n        \"Suggests performance optimizations\",\n        \"Checks code style and consistency\",\n        \"Recommends best practices\",\n        \"Provides constructive feedback\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Code Review\", \"Bug Detection\", \"Style Checking\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Code Review Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ci-fixer\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a CI Fixer\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps fix CI/CD pipeline failures and test errors.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Analyzes CI/CD error messages and logs\",\n        \"Identifies root causes of failures\",\n        \"Suggests fixes for test failures\",\n        \"Helps resolve dependency conflicts\",\n        \"Provides step-by-step resolution guidance\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"CI/CD Integration\", \"Test Fixing\", \"Error Resolution\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"CI/CD Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"knowledge-retriever\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor searches through your codebase to find relevant information.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Searches across files and directories\",\n        \"Finds related code and documentation\",\n        \"Understands code relationships\",\n        \"Retrieves context for questions\",\n        \"Helps navigate large codebases\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Code Search\", \"Context Retrieval\", \"Codebase Navigation\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Search Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"refactoring-assistant\",\n      \"title\": \"Cursor as a Refactoring Assistant\",\n      \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps improve code structure without changing functionality.\",\n      \"detailedExplanation\": [\n        \"Suggests structural improvements\",\n        \"Identifies code duplication\",\n        \"Recommends design pattern applications\",\n        \"Helps extract reusable components\",\n        \"Maintains functionality while improving code quality\"\n      ],\n      \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Refactoring\", \"Code Quality\", \"Design Patterns\"],\n      \"docs\": [\n        { \"label\": \"Refactoring Guide\", \"url\": \"#\" }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-05 21:18:27] {"conversation_id":"1d95a7c0-f530-43e4-90c1-fef078437daa","generation_id":"4726535c-094f-41d8-ad61-7a2bb9b6b908","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/index.html","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Cursor Mental Models – AI Terms Dictionary</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <h1>Cursor Mental Models</h1>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">AI Terms Dictionary</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <main>\n        <div class=\"search-container\">\n            <input \n                type=\"text\" \n                id=\"search-input\" \n                placeholder=\"Search mental models...\" \n                aria-label=\"Search mental models\"\n            >\n        </div>\n\n        <div id=\"cards-container\" class=\"cards-grid\">\n            <!-- Cards will be dynamically inserted here -->\n        </div>\n\n        <div id=\"no-results\" class=\"no-results\" style=\"display: none;\">\n            <p>No mental models found matching your search.</p>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <!-- Modal Overlay -->\n    <div id=\"modal-overlay\" class=\"modal-overlay\" style=\"display: none;\">\n        <div class=\"modal-content\">\n            <button id=\"modal-close\" class=\"modal-close\" aria-label=\"Close modal\">×</button>\n            <div id=\"modal-body\">\n                <!-- Modal content will be dynamically inserted here -->\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <noscript>\n        <div class=\"no-js-message\">\n            <p>This site requires JavaScript to function. Please enable JavaScript in your browser.</p>\n        </div>\n    </noscript>\n\n    <script src=\"app.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-05 21:18:34] {"conversation_id":"1d95a7c0-f530-43e4-90c1-fef078437daa","generation_id":"4726535c-094f-41d8-ad61-7a2bb9b6b908","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/styles.css","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"/* Design System - CSS Custom Properties */\n:root {\n    --bg-color: #f5f5f5;\n    --card-bg: white;\n    --text-primary: #222;\n    --text-secondary: #333;\n    --text-muted: #666;\n    --accent-color: #4f8cff;\n    --tag-bg: #e3f0ff;\n    --tag-text: #1e5fcc;\n    --shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n    --shadow-hover: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);\n    --spacing-xs: 8px;\n    --spacing-sm: 16px;\n    --spacing-md: 24px;\n    --spacing-lg: 32px;\n    --spacing-xl: 48px;\n    --border-radius: 8px;\n}\n\n/* Base Typography and Reset */\n* {\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n\nbody {\n    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;\n    background-color: var(--bg-color);\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);\n}\n\n/* Header Styles */\nheader {\n    background-color: var(--card-bg);\n    padding: var(--spacing-lg) var(--spacing-md);\n    text-align: center;\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 4px var(--shadow);\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);\n}\n\nheader h1 {\n    font-size: 2.5rem;\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);\n    font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.subtitle {\n    font-size: 1.1rem;\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n    font-weight: 400;\n}\n\n/* Search Container */\n.search-container {\n    max-width: 1200px;\n    margin: 0 auto var(--spacing-lg);\n    padding: 0 var(--spacing-md);\n}\n\n#search-input {\n    width: 100%;\n    max-width: 600px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    display: block;\n    padding: var(--spacing-sm);\n    font-size: 1rem;\n    border: 2px solid #ddd;\n    border-radius: var(--border-radius);\n    background-color: var(--card-bg);\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    transition: border-color 0.2s;\n}\n\n#search-input:focus {\n    outline: none;\n    border-color: var(--accent-color);\n}\n\n#search-input::placeholder {\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n/* Cards Grid Layout */\n.cards-grid {\n    max-width: 1200px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 0 var(--spacing-md);\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));\n    gap: var(--spacing-md);\n}\n\n/* Card Styles */\n.card {\n    background-color: var(--card-bg);\n    border-radius: var(--border-radius);\n    padding: var(--spacing-md);\n    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px var(--shadow);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;\n}\n\n.card:hover {\n    transform: translateY(-2px);\n    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px var(--shadow-hover);\n}\n\n.card-title {\n    font-size: 1.5rem;\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);\n    font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.card-description {\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);\n    line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n/* Feature Tags */\n.card-tags {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    gap: var(--spacing-xs);\n}\n\n.tag {\n    display: inline-block;\n    padding: 4px 12px;\n    background-color: var(--tag-bg);\n    color: var(--tag-text);\n    border-radius: 16px;\n    font-size: 0.875rem;\n    font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n/* No Results Message */\n.no-results {\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: var(--spacing-xl);\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n    font-size: 1.1rem;\n}\n\n/* Modal Overlay */\n.modal-overlay {\n    position: fixed;\n    top: 0;\n    left: 0;\n    right: 0;\n    bottom: 0;\n    background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    z-index: 1000;\n    padding: var(--spacing-md);\n    overflow-y: auto;\n}\n\n.modal-content {\n    background-color: var(--card-bg);\n    border-radius: var(--border-radius);\n    padding: var(--spacing-lg);\n    max-width: 700px;\n    width: 100%;\n    max-height: 90vh;\n    overflow-y: auto;\n    position: relative;\n    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);\n}\n\n.modal-close {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: var(--spacing-md);\n    right: var(--spacing-md);\n    background: none;\n    border: none;\n    font-size: 2rem;\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    width: 32px;\n    height: 32px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    transition: background-color 0.2s;\n}\n\n.modal-close:hover {\n    background-color: var(--bg-color);\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n}\n\n.modal-title {\n    font-size: 2rem;\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);\n    padding-right: var(--spacing-xl);\n    font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.modal-section {\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);\n}\n\n.modal-section-title {\n    font-size: 1.2rem;\n    color: var(--text-secondary);\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);\n    font-weight: 600;\n}\n\n.modal-explanation {\n    list-style: none;\n    padding-left: 0;\n}\n\n.modal-explanation li {\n    padding: var(--spacing-xs) 0;\n    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);\n    position: relative;\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n.modal-explanation li::before {\n    content: \"•\";\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    color: var(--accent-color);\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n.modal-features {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    gap: var(--spacing-xs);\n}\n\n.modal-docs {\n    list-style: none;\n    padding-left: 0;\n}\n\n.modal-docs li {\n    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);\n}\n\n.modal-docs a {\n    color: var(--accent-color);\n    text-decoration: none;\n    font-weight: 500;\n}\n\n.modal-docs a:hover {\n    text-decoration: underline;\n}\n\n/* No JavaScript Message */\n.no-js-message {\n    text-align: center;\n    padding: var(--spacing-xl);\n    background-color: #fff3cd;\n    color: #856404;\n    margin: var(--spacing-md);\n    border-radius: var(--border-radius);\n}\n\n/* Responsive Breakpoints */\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    header h1 {\n        font-size: 2rem;\n    }\n\n    .subtitle {\n        font-size: 1rem;\n    }\n\n    .cards-grid {\n        grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n        gap: var(--spacing-sm);\n    }\n\n    .modal-content {\n        padding: var(--spacing-md);\n        margin: var(--spacing-sm);\n    }\n\n    .modal-title {\n        font-size: 1.5rem;\n    }\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 480px) {\n    header {\n        padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-sm);\n    }\n\n    header h1 {\n        font-size: 1.75rem;\n    }\n\n    .search-container {\n        padding: 0 var(--spacing-sm);\n    }\n\n    .cards-grid {\n        padding: 0 var(--spacing-sm);\n    }\n\n    .card {\n        padding: var(--spacing-sm);\n    }\n}\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-05 21:18:41] {"conversation_id":"1d95a7c0-f530-43e4-90c1-fef078437daa","generation_id":"4726535c-094f-41d8-ad61-7a2bb9b6b908","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/app.js","edits":[{"old_string":"// Global state\nlet allModels = [];\nlet currentFilteredModels = [];\n\n// DOM elements\nconst searchInput = document.getElementById('search-input');\nconst cardsContainer = document.getElementById('cards-container');\nconst noResults = document.getElementById('no-results');\nconst errorMessage = document.getElementById('error-message');\nconst modalOverlay = document.getElementById('modal-overlay');\nconst modalBody = document.getElementById('modal-body');\nconst modalClose = document.getElementById('modal-close');\n\n// Load data from JSON file\nasync function loadData() {\n    try {\n        const response = await fetch('data/mental-models.json');\n        if (!response.ok) {\n            throw new Error(`Failed to load data: ${response.status} ${response.statusText}`);\n        }\n        allModels = await response.json();\n        currentFilteredModels = allModels;\n        renderCards(allModels);\n    } catch (error) {\n        console.error('Error loading data:', error);\n        errorMessage.textContent = `Error: Unable to load mental models data. ${error.message}`;\n        errorMessage.style.display = 'block';\n        cardsContainer.style.display = 'none';\n    }\n}\n\n// Create a single card element\nfunction renderCard(model) {\n    const card = document.createElement('div');\n    card.className = 'card';\n    card.setAttribute('data-id', model.id);\n    \n    const title = document.createElement('h2');\n    title.className = 'card-title';\n    title.textContent = model.title;\n    \n    const description = document.createElement('p');\n    description.className = 'card-description';\n    description.textContent = model.shortDescription;\n    \n    const featuresContainer = document.createElement('div');\n    featuresContainer.className = 'card-features';\n    \n    model.relatedFeatures.forEach(feature => {\n        const tag = document.createElement('span');\n        tag.className = 'feature-tag';\n        tag.textContent = feature;\n        featuresContainer.appendChild(tag);\n    });\n    \n    card.appendChild(title);\n    card.appendChild(description);\n    card.appendChild(featuresContainer);\n    \n    // Add click handler\n    card.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        openModal(model);\n    });\n    \n    return card;\n}\n\n// Render all cards\nfunction renderCards(models) {\n    cardsContainer.innerHTML = '';\n    noResults.style.display = 'none';\n    \n    if (models.length === 0) {\n        noResults.style.display = 'block';\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    models.forEach(model => {\n        const card = renderCard(model);\n        cardsContainer.appendChild(card);\n    });\n}\n\n// Handle search input\nfunction handleSearch(query) {\n    const searchTerm = query.trim().toLowerCase();\n    \n    if (searchTerm === '') {\n        currentFilteredModels = allModels;\n        renderCards(allModels);\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    currentFilteredModels = allModels.filter(model => {\n        const titleMatch = model.title.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm);\n        const descMatch = model.shortDescription.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm);\n        return titleMatch || descMatch;\n    });\n    \n    renderCards(currentFilteredModels);\n}\n\n// Open modal with model details\nfunction openModal(model) {\n    modalOverlay.style.display = 'flex';\n    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';\n    \n    const title = document.createElement('h2');\n    title.id = 'modal-title';\n    title.className = 'modal-title';\n    title.textContent = model.title;\n    \n    const explanation = document.createElement('div');\n    explanation.className = 'modal-explanation';\n    const explanationList = document.createElement('ul');\n    model.detailedExplanation.forEach(point => {\n        const li = document.createElement('li');\n        li.textContent = point;\n        explanationList.appendChild(li);\n    });\n    explanation.appendChild(explanationList);\n    \n    const features = document.createElement('div');\n    features.className = 'modal-features';\n    const featuresTitle = document.createElement('h3');\n    featuresTitle.textContent = 'Related Features:';\n    features.appendChild(featuresTitle);\n    const featuresContainer = document.createElement('div');\n    featuresContainer.className = 'modal-features-tags';\n    model.relatedFeatures.forEach(feature => {\n        const tag = document.createElement('span');\n        tag.className = 'feature-tag';\n        tag.textContent = feature;\n        featuresContainer.appendChild(tag);\n    });\n    features.appendChild(featuresContainer);\n    \n    const docs = document.createElement('div');\n    docs.className = 'modal-docs';\n    const docsTitle = document.createElement('h3');\n    docsTitle.textContent = 'Documentation:';\n    docs.appendChild(docsTitle);\n    const docsList = document.createElement('ul');\n    docsList.className = 'modal-docs-list';\n    model.docs.forEach(doc => {\n        const li = document.createElement('li');\n        const link = document.createElement('a');\n        link.href = doc.url;\n        link.target = '_blank';\n        link.rel = 'noopener noreferrer';\n        link.textContent = doc.label;\n        li.appendChild(link);\n        docsList.appendChild(li);\n    });\n    docs.appendChild(docsList);\n    \n    modalBody.innerHTML = '';\n    modalBody.appendChild(title);\n    modalBody.appendChild(explanation);\n    modalBody.appendChild(features);\n    modalBody.appendChild(docs);\n    \n    // Focus management for accessibility\n    modalClose.focus();\n}\n\n// Close modal\nfunction closeModal() {\n    modalOverlay.style.display = 'none';\n    document.body.style.overflow = '';\n    modalBody.innerHTML = '';\n}\n\n// Event listeners\nsearchInput.addEventListener('input', (e) => {\n    handleSearch(e.target.value);\n});\n\nmodalClose.addEventListener('click', () => {\n    closeModal();\n});\n\nmodalOverlay.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n    if (e.target === modalOverlay) {\n        closeModal();\n    }\n});\n\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n    if (e.key === 'Escape' && modalOverlay.style.display === 'flex') {\n        closeModal();\n    }\n});\n\n// Initialize on page load\nloadData();\n\n","new_string":"// State Management\nlet mentalModels = [];\nlet filteredModels = [];\nlet currentModalId = null;\n\n// DOM Elements\nconst cardsContainer = document.getElementById('cards-container');\nconst searchInput = document.getElementById('search-input');\nconst modalOverlay = document.getElementById('modal-overlay');\nconst modalBody = document.getElementById('modal-body');\nconst modalClose = document.getElementById('modal-close');\nconst noResults = document.getElementById('no-results');\n\n// Load data from JSON file\nasync function loadData() {\n    try {\n        const response = await fetch('data/mental-models.json');\n        if (!response.ok) {\n            throw new Error('Failed to load mental models data');\n        }\n        const data = await response.json();\n        mentalModels = data.mentalModels || [];\n        filteredModels = [...mentalModels];\n        renderCards();\n    } catch (error) {\n        console.error('Error loading data:', error);\n        cardsContainer.innerHTML = '<p style=\"text-align: center; color: #666;\">Error loading mental models. Please refresh the page.</p>';\n    }\n}\n\n// Render cards in the grid\nfunction renderCards() {\n    cardsContainer.innerHTML = '';\n    \n    if (filteredModels.length === 0) {\n        noResults.style.display = 'block';\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    noResults.style.display = 'none';\n    \n    filteredModels.forEach(model => {\n        const card = createCardElement(model);\n        cardsContainer.appendChild(card);\n    });\n}\n\n// Create a card DOM element\nfunction createCardElement(model) {\n    const card = document.createElement('div');\n    card.className = 'card';\n    card.setAttribute('data-id', model.id);\n    \n    const title = document.createElement('h2');\n    title.className = 'card-title';\n    title.textContent = model.title;\n    \n    const description = document.createElement('p');\n    description.className = 'card-description';\n    description.textContent = model.shortDescription;\n    \n    const tagsContainer = document.createElement('div');\n    tagsContainer.className = 'card-tags';\n    \n    if (model.relatedFeatures && model.relatedFeatures.length > 0) {\n        model.relatedFeatures.forEach(feature => {\n            const tag = document.createElement('span');\n            tag.className = 'tag';\n            tag.textContent = feature;\n            tagsContainer.appendChild(tag);\n        });\n    }\n    \n    card.appendChild(title);\n    card.appendChild(description);\n    card.appendChild(tagsContainer);\n    \n    // Add click handler\n    card.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        openModal(model.id);\n    });\n    \n    return card;\n}\n\n// Filter cards based on search term\nfunction filterCards(searchTerm) {\n    const term = searchTerm.toLowerCase().trim();\n    \n    if (term === '') {\n        filteredModels = [...mentalModels];\n    } else {\n        filteredModels = mentalModels.filter(model => {\n            const titleMatch = model.title.toLowerCase().includes(term);\n            const descMatch = model.shortDescription.toLowerCase().includes(term);\n            const featuresMatch = model.relatedFeatures.some(feature => \n                feature.toLowerCase().includes(term)\n            );\n            return titleMatch || descMatch || featuresMatch;\n        });\n    }\n    \n    renderCards();\n}\n\n// Open modal with model details\nfunction openModal(modelId) {\n    const model = mentalModels.find(m => m.id === modelId);\n    if (!model) {\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    currentModalId = modelId;\n    \n    // Build modal content\n    let html = `\n        <h2 class=\"modal-title\">${escapeHtml(model.title)}</h2>\n    `;\n    \n    // Detailed explanation\n    if (model.detailedExplanation && model.detailedExplanation.length > 0) {\n        html += `\n            <div class=\"modal-section\">\n                <h3 class=\"modal-section-title\">Detailed Explanation</h3>\n                <ul class=\"modal-explanation\">\n        `;\n        model.detailedExplanation.forEach(point => {\n            html += `<li>${escapeHtml(point)}</li>`;\n        });\n        html += `\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        `;\n    }\n    \n    // Related features\n    if (model.relatedFeatures && model.relatedFeatures.length > 0) {\n        html += `\n            <div class=\"modal-section\">\n                <h3 class=\"modal-section-title\">Related Features</h3>\n                <div class=\"modal-features\">\n        `;\n        model.relatedFeatures.forEach(feature => {\n            html += `<span class=\"tag\">${escapeHtml(feature)}</span>`;\n        });\n        html += `\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        `;\n    }\n    \n    // Documentation links\n    if (model.docs && model.docs.length > 0) {\n        html += `\n            <div class=\"modal-section\">\n                <h3 class=\"modal-section-title\">Documentation</h3>\n                <ul class=\"modal-docs\">\n        `;\n        model.docs.forEach(doc => {\n            html += `<li><a href=\"${escapeHtml(doc.url)}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">${escapeHtml(doc.label)}</a></li>`;\n        });\n        html += `\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        `;\n    }\n    \n    modalBody.innerHTML = html;\n    modalOverlay.style.display = 'flex';\n    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';\n}\n\n// Close modal\nfunction closeModal() {\n    modalOverlay.style.display = 'none';\n    currentModalId = null;\n    document.body.style.overflow = '';\n}\n\n// Escape HTML to prevent XSS\nfunction escapeHtml(text) {\n    const div = document.createElement('div');\n    div.textContent = text;\n    return div.innerHTML;\n}\n\n// Initialize the application\nfunction init() {\n    // Search input event listener\n    searchInput.addEventListener('input', (e) => {\n        filterCards(e.target.value);\n    });\n    \n    // Modal close handlers\n    modalClose.addEventListener('click', closeModal);\n    \n    modalOverlay.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n        if (e.target === modalOverlay) {\n            closeModal();\n        }\n    });\n    \n    // Escape key handler\n    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n        if (e.key === 'Escape' && currentModalId !== null) {\n            closeModal();\n        }\n    });\n    \n    // Load data\n    loadData();\n}\n\n// Start the app when DOM is ready\nif (document.readyState === 'loading') {\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);\n} else {\n    init();\n}\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-05 21:18:44] {"conversation_id":"1d95a7c0-f530-43e4-90c1-fef078437daa","generation_id":"4726535c-094f-41d8-ad61-7a2bb9b6b908","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/README.md","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"# Cursor Mental Models – AI Terms Dictionary\n\nA minimal static website that explains how to think about Cursor using high-level mental models. Each mental model represents a conceptual role that Cursor can play in your development workflow.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis is a **demo project** created for a live presentation about Cursor. It demonstrates how to conceptualize Cursor's capabilities through mental models like:\n\n- Cursor as a Planner\n- Cursor as a Pair Programmer\n- Cursor as a Code Reviewer\n- Cursor as a CI Fixer\n- Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever\n- Cursor as a Refactoring Assistant\n\n## What Are Mental Models?\n\nMental models are conceptual frameworks that help you understand how to use Cursor effectively. Instead of thinking about Cursor as a single tool, you can think of it playing different roles depending on your needs. Each mental model represents a different way to interact with and leverage Cursor's capabilities.\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/\n├── index.html              # Main HTML structure\n├── styles.css             # All styling\n├── app.js                 # JavaScript logic\n├── data/\n│   └── mental-models.json # Mental model data\n└── README.md             # This file\n```\n\n## Running Locally\n\nThis is a **static website** with no build step or dependencies. To run it:\n\n1. Open `index.html` in your web browser\n2. That's it!\n\n**Note:** Due to browser security restrictions, you may need to serve the files through a local web server instead of opening the file directly. You can use:\n\n- Python: `python -m http.server 8000` (then visit `http://localhost:8000`)\n- Node.js: `npx http-server` (then visit the URL shown)\n- Or any other simple HTTP server\n\n## Features\n\n- **Interactive Card Grid**: Browse mental models as cards\n- **Search**: Filter mental models by title, description, or features\n- **Modal Details**: Click any card to see detailed information\n- **Responsive Design**: Works on desktop, tablet, and mobile devices\n- **No Dependencies**: Pure HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript\n\n## Technical Details\n\n- Plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript (no frameworks)\n- No build tools or bundlers\n- No backend or external services\n- All content loaded from JSON\n- Progressive enhancement (works without JavaScript, but shows a message)\n\n## Adding Mental Models\n\nTo add new mental models, edit `data/mental-models.json` and add entries following this structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"unique-id\",\n  \"title\": \"Model Title\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Brief description\",\n  \"detailedExplanation\": [\"Point 1\", \"Point 2\"],\n  \"relatedFeatures\": [\"Feature 1\", \"Feature 2\"],\n  \"docs\": [\n    { \"label\": \"Link Text\", \"url\": \"https://example.com\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Demo Context\n\nThis project is intentionally simple and static to demonstrate Cursor's capabilities in a presentation setting. It prioritizes clarity and readability over complex engineering.\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
