[2026-01-05 21:45:38] {"conversation_id":"dffcaa2f-0d39-49c7-a8b6-521c8bb28b23","generation_id":"a25cb54c-ad11-4201-993d-2cd623c734ad","model":"gpt-5.1-codex-fast","file_path":"/Users/tamar/.cursor/worktrees/cursor-mental-models-demo/juf/e2e-tests.md","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"# Cursor Mental Models – End-to-End Test\n\nThis project runs without a build step, so the E2E flow is intentionally simple and manual-friendly. The checklist below verifies the most important user journeys using just a static file server and a browser.\n\n## Setup\n1. Start any static server from the project root, e.g. `python -m http.server 8000`.\n2. Visit `http://localhost:8000` in a modern desktop browser.\n3. Ensure the DevTools console is open to watch for runtime errors.\n\n## Test Cases\n\n### 1. Page load shows all mental models\n- Refresh the page.\n- **Expect:** Hero title, subtitle, and search field are visible.\n- **Expect:** Six cards render (Planner, Pair Programmer, Code Reviewer, CI Fixer, Knowledge Retriever, Refactoring Assistant).\n- **Expect:** No errors appear in the console.\n\n### 2. Search filters cards by title and description\n- Type `planner` into the search input.\n- **Expect:** Only the “Cursor as a Planner” card remains.\n- Clear the search, then type `code`.\n- **Expect:** Cards whose title or description contains “code” (Pair Programmer, Code Reviewer, Refactoring Assistant) stay visible while others hide.\n\n### 3. Modal opens with full detail\n- Clear the search so all cards return.\n- Click the “Cursor as a CI Fixer” card.\n- **Expect:** The modal overlay fades in, the backdrop locks scroll, and the modal header matches the card title.\n- **Expect:** Five bullet points render under “Detailed Explanation”, feature tags appear, and at least one docs link is rendered.\n\n### 4. Modal closes via all supported interactions\n- With the modal still open, click the “×” close button.\n- **Expect:** Modal hides and focus returns to the previously selected card.\n- Re-open any modal, press the `Esc` key, and **expect** it closes.\n- Re-open again, click on the dark overlay outside the modal, and **expect** it closes without console errors.\n\n### 5. Documentation links open safely\n- Open a modal (any card) and click its documentation link.\n- **Expect:** Link opens in a new tab/window (default browser behavior for `target=\"_blank\"`).\n- Close the modal afterward.\n\n### 6. Error banner appears if data fails to load\n- Temporarily rename `data/mental-models.json` to simulate a fetch failure, then reload the page.\n- **Expect:** Instead of cards, a friendly error message displays in the cards container.\n- Restore the file name when finished.\n\nCompleting all six cases confirms the key end-to-end paths: initial load, search, rich detail display, modal interactions, external doc link handling, and fallback behavior when data is unavailable.\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
