[2026-01-13 21:08:13] {"conversation_id":"93d4c15e-e313-4e59-a9c9-f6097d6dc098","generation_id":"6eb9ccf3-2ecc-4c1a-8e71-ac83dacc6026","model":"composer-1","prompt":"You are building a small, static demo website intended for a live presentation about Cursor.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- This is a DEMO project, not a production app.\n- Keep everything extremely simple, explicit, and readable.\n- Prefer clarity over cleverness.\n- Do NOT introduce any backend, frameworks, build tools, or external services.\n- Everything must work by opening index.html locally.\n- Assume the audience is non-frontend developers.\n\n--------------------------------------------\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\n--------------------------------------------\n\nCreate a minimal static website called:\n\n\"Cursor Mental Models – AI Terms Dictionary\"\n\nThe purpose of this site is to explain how to THINK about Cursor,\nusing high-level mental models (conceptual roles Cursor can play).\n\nEach card represents one mental model.\n\nExamples:\n- Cursor as a Planner\n- Cursor as a Pair Programmer\n- Cursor as a Code Reviewer\n- Cursor as a CI Fixer\n- Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever\n\n--------------------------------------------\nTECH STACK (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------\n\n- Plain HTML\n- Plain CSS\n- Vanilla JavaScript\n- No React / Vue / frameworks\n- No backend\n- No APIs\n- No external libraries\n- No build step\n\n--------------------------------------------\nFILE STRUCTURE\n--------------------------------------------\n\nCreate exactly this structure:\n\n/index.html\n/styles.css\n/app.js\n/data/mental-models.json\n/README.md\n\n--------------------------------------------\nDATA MODEL\n--------------------------------------------\n\nALL content must come from a single JSON file:\ndata/mental-models.json\n\nEach mental model object must include:\n\n- id (string, unique)\n- title (string)\n- shortDescription (1–2 sentences)\n- detailedExplanation (array of bullet points, strings)\n- relatedFeatures (array of strings)\n- docs (array of objects: { label, url })\n\n--------------------------------------------\nUI & DESIGN REQUIREMENTS\n--------------------------------------------\n\nLayout:\n- Single-page layout\n- Header with title + subtitle\n- Search input below header\n- Grid of cards below\n\nCards:\n- White background\n- Rounded corners\n- Soft shadow\n- Title, short description, feature tags\n\nInteraction:\n- Clicking a card opens a modal overlay\n- Modal shows:\n  - Title\n  - Detailed explanation (bullets)\n  - Related feature tags\n  - Documentation links\n\nDesign system:\n- Background: very light gray (#f5f5f5)\n- Cards: white\n- Primary text: dark gray (#222/#333)\n- Secondary text: muted gray (#666)\n- Accent color: soft blue (#4f8cff)\n- Feature tags: light blue background, darker blue text\n- System fonts only\n- Generous spacing, calm layout\n\n--------------------------------------------\nBEHAVIOR REQUIREMENTS\n--------------------------------------------\n\n- Load data dynamically from mental-models.json\n- No hardcoded content in HTML\n- No inline styles\n- JavaScript handles:\n  - Data loading\n  - Rendering cards\n  - Case-insensitive search\n  - Modal open / close\n\n--------------------------------------------\nREADME REQUIREMENTS\n--------------------------------------------\n\nREADME.md should briefly explain:\n- What the project is\n- That it is a demo for a live Cursor presentation\n- That the site is intentionally static\n- How to run it locally\n- What mental models represent conceptually\n\n--------------------------------------------\nDELIVERABLE INSTRUCTIONS\n--------------------------------------------\n\nSTEP 1 — PLAN  \nProduce a clear, structured PLAN that includes:\n- File responsibilities\n- Data flow (JSON → JS → UI)\n- Interaction flow\n\nSTEP 2 — TODO LIST  \nAfter the plan, produce an explicit TODO checklist:\n- 10–15 items\n- Ordered\n- Each item should be a concrete, actionable step\n- Example: \"Create index.html skeleton\", \"Implement loadData() in app.js\"\n- Do NOT write any code yet\n\nSTEP 3 — QUESTIONS  \nIf anything is ambiguous or requires clarification,\nask concise clarification questions BEFORE writing code.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do NOT implement anything yet.\n- Wait for explicit confirmation before writing code.\n\n","attachments":[{"type":"file","file_path":"/Users/tamar/.cursor/projects/Users-tamar-cursor-mental-models-demo/terminals/1.txt"},{"type":"rule","file_path":"demo-always-apply.mdc"}],"hook_event_name":"beforeSubmitPrompt","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
