[2026-01-13 21:10:56] {"conversation_id":"93d4c15e-e313-4e59-a9c9-f6097d6dc098","generation_id":"f5c4a760-9ee1-44b2-8242-0f4be3a763ff","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/data/mental-models.json","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-planner\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Planner\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps break down complex tasks into manageable steps, creating structured plans before implementation.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor analyzes your request and decomposes it into logical, sequential steps\",\n      \"It identifies dependencies between tasks and suggests an optimal order of execution\",\n      \"The planning phase helps catch potential issues before coding begins\",\n      \"Plans can be reviewed and refined through conversation before implementation\",\n      \"This mental model emphasizes thinking before doing, reducing wasted effort\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Composer\",\n      \"Chat\",\n      \"Multi-file editing\",\n      \"Code generation\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Documentation\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-pair-programmer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Pair Programmer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor acts as a collaborative coding partner, discussing approaches, reviewing code, and suggesting improvements in real-time.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor engages in back-and-forth dialogue about code design and implementation choices\",\n      \"It provides context-aware suggestions based on your codebase and coding style\",\n      \"Like a human pair programmer, it asks clarifying questions when requirements are ambiguous\",\n      \"It can explain its reasoning and adapt to your feedback during the conversation\",\n      \"This collaborative approach leads to better solutions than one-way code generation\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Chat\",\n      \"Codebase context\",\n      \"Inline suggestions\",\n      \"Code explanations\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Chat Features\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/chat\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-code-reviewer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Code Reviewer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor examines code for bugs, style issues, security vulnerabilities, and opportunities for improvement.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor reviews code with a focus on correctness, maintainability, and best practices\",\n      \"It identifies potential bugs, edge cases, and security concerns before they reach production\",\n      \"The review process considers code style, naming conventions, and architectural patterns\",\n      \"It provides constructive feedback with explanations, not just error messages\",\n      \"This mental model helps maintain code quality and catch issues early in development\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Code analysis\",\n      \"Error detection\",\n      \"Style suggestions\",\n      \"Security scanning\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Code Review\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/review\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-ci-fixer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a CI Fixer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor automatically diagnoses and fixes CI/CD pipeline failures, test errors, and build issues.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"When CI fails, Cursor analyzes error messages, logs, and test outputs to identify root causes\",\n      \"It suggests specific fixes for broken tests, compilation errors, and configuration issues\",\n      \"Cursor understands the relationship between code changes and CI failures\",\n      \"It can fix multiple related issues in a single pass, not just one error at a time\",\n      \"This mental model treats CI as a feedback loop that Cursor helps resolve efficiently\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Error analysis\",\n      \"Test fixing\",\n      \"Build debugging\",\n      \"Multi-file changes\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"CI Integration\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/ci\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-knowledge-retriever\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor searches through your codebase, documentation, and context to find relevant information and answer questions.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor indexes and understands your entire codebase, making information retrieval fast and accurate\",\n      \"It can answer questions about how code works, where features are implemented, and what patterns are used\",\n      \"The retrieval process considers context, not just keyword matching\",\n      \"It synthesizes information from multiple files and sources to provide comprehensive answers\",\n      \"This mental model positions Cursor as a searchable knowledge base of your project\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Codebase indexing\",\n      \"Semantic search\",\n      \"Context awareness\",\n      \"Documentation lookup\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Codebase Context\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/context\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:10:59] {"conversation_id":"93d4c15e-e313-4e59-a9c9-f6097d6dc098","generation_id":"f5c4a760-9ee1-44b2-8242-0f4be3a763ff","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/app.js","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"// Global state\nlet allModels = [];\nlet filteredModels = [];\n\n// Load data from JSON file\nasync function loadData() {\n    try {\n        const response = await fetch('data/mental-models.json');\n        if (!response.ok) {\n            throw new Error(`Failed to load data: ${response.status}`);\n        }\n        allModels = await response.json();\n        filteredModels = allModels;\n        renderCards(filteredModels);\n    } catch (error) {\n        console.error('Error loading data:', error);\n        const container = document.getElementById('cards-container');\n        container.innerHTML = '<p style=\"color: #d32f2f; text-align: center; padding: 2rem;\">Failed to load mental models. Please check that data/mental-models.json exists.</p>';\n    }\n}\n\n// Render cards grid\nfunction renderCards(models) {\n    const container = document.getElementById('cards-container');\n    \n    if (models.length === 0) {\n        container.innerHTML = '<p style=\"color: #666; text-align: center; padding: 2rem;\">No mental models found matching your search.</p>';\n        return;\n    }\n\n    container.innerHTML = models.map(model => `\n        <div class=\"card\" data-id=\"${model.id}\">\n            <h2 class=\"card-title\">${escapeHtml(model.title)}</h2>\n            <p class=\"card-description\">${escapeHtml(model.shortDescription)}</p>\n            <div class=\"card-features\">\n                ${model.relatedFeatures.slice(0, 3).map(feature => \n                    `<span class=\"feature-tag\">${escapeHtml(feature)}</span>`\n                ).join('')}\n                ${model.relatedFeatures.length > 3 ? `<span class=\"feature-tag\">+${model.relatedFeatures.length - 3} more</span>` : ''}\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    `).join('');\n\n    // Attach click handlers to cards\n    container.querySelectorAll('.card').forEach(card => {\n        card.addEventListener('click', () => {\n            const modelId = card.getAttribute('data-id');\n            const model = allModels.find(m => m.id === modelId);\n            if (model) {\n                openModal(model);\n            }\n        });\n    });\n}\n\n// Render modal content\nfunction renderModal(model) {\n    const modalBody = document.getElementById('modal-body');\n    \n    modalBody.innerHTML = `\n        <h2 class=\"modal-title\">${escapeHtml(model.title)}</h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"modal-explanation\">\n            <ul>\n                ${model.detailedExplanation.map(point => \n                    `<li>${escapeHtml(point)}</li>`\n                ).join('')}\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"modal-features\">\n            <div class=\"modal-features-title\">Related Features:</div>\n            <div class=\"card-features\">\n                ${model.relatedFeatures.map(feature => \n                    `<span class=\"feature-tag\">${escapeHtml(feature)}</span>`\n                ).join('')}\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        ${model.docs && model.docs.length > 0 ? `\n            <div class=\"modal-docs\">\n                <div class=\"modal-docs-title\">Documentation:</div>\n                <ul class=\"modal-docs-list\">\n                    ${model.docs.map(doc => \n                        `<li><a href=\"${escapeHtml(doc.url)}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">${escapeHtml(doc.label)}</a></li>`\n                    ).join('')}\n                </ul>\n            </div>\n        ` : ''}\n    `;\n}\n\n// Open modal with model data\nfunction openModal(model) {\n    renderModal(model);\n    const overlay = document.getElementById('modal-overlay');\n    overlay.classList.remove('hidden');\n    \n    // Prevent body scroll when modal is open\n    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';\n}\n\n// Close modal\nfunction closeModal() {\n    const overlay = document.getElementById('modal-overlay');\n    overlay.classList.add('hidden');\n    \n    // Restore body scroll\n    document.body.style.overflow = '';\n}\n\n// Handle search input\nfunction handleSearch(query) {\n    const searchTerm = query.trim().toLowerCase();\n    \n    if (searchTerm === '') {\n        filteredModels = allModels;\n    } else {\n        filteredModels = allModels.filter(model => \n            model.title.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm)\n        );\n    }\n    \n    renderCards(filteredModels);\n}\n\n// Escape HTML to prevent XSS\nfunction escapeHtml(text) {\n    const div = document.createElement('div');\n    div.textContent = text;\n    return div.innerHTML;\n}\n\n// Initialize on page load\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n    // Load data\n    loadData();\n\n    // Search input handler\n    const searchInput = document.getElementById('search-input');\n    searchInput.addEventListener('input', (e) => {\n        handleSearch(e.target.value);\n    });\n\n    // Modal close handlers\n    const modalOverlay = document.getElementById('modal-overlay');\n    const modalClose = document.querySelector('.modal-close');\n\n    modalClose.addEventListener('click', closeModal);\n\n    modalOverlay.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n        // Close if clicking the overlay (not the modal content)\n        if (e.target === modalOverlay) {\n            closeModal();\n        }\n    });\n\n    // Close modal on Escape key\n    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n        if (e.key === 'Escape' && !modalOverlay.classList.contains('hidden')) {\n            closeModal();\n        }\n    });\n});\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:11:01] {"conversation_id":"93d4c15e-e313-4e59-a9c9-f6097d6dc098","generation_id":"f5c4a760-9ee1-44b2-8242-0f4be3a763ff","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/README.md","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"# Cursor Mental Models – AI Terms Dictionary\n\nA minimal static website demo for live Cursor presentations that explains how to think about Cursor using high-level mental models.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis site demonstrates conceptual roles that Cursor can play in software development. Each mental model card represents a different way to understand and interact with Cursor:\n\n- **Cursor as a Planner** – Breaking down complex tasks into manageable steps\n- **Cursor as a Pair Programmer** – Collaborative coding partner\n- **Cursor as a Code Reviewer** – Examining code for quality and issues\n- **Cursor as a CI Fixer** – Diagnosing and fixing CI/CD failures\n- **Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever** – Searching and understanding codebases\n\nMental models help developers understand when and how to use Cursor effectively by providing conceptual frameworks for different use cases.\n\n## Tech Stack\n\nThis is intentionally a **static demo** with no build tools or frameworks:\n\n- Plain HTML\n- Plain CSS\n- Vanilla JavaScript\n- No backend, APIs, or external services\n- No build step required\n\n## Running Locally\n\nSimply open `index.html` in your web browser. That's it!\n\nThe site loads data from `data/mental-models.json` and renders it dynamically.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Card Grid View** – Browse all mental models at a glance\n- **Search** – Filter models by title (case-insensitive)\n- **Modal Details** – Click any card to see full explanation, features, and documentation links\n- **Responsive Design** – Works on desktop and mobile devices\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/\n├── index.html          # Main HTML structure\n├── styles.css          # All styling\n├── app.js              # JavaScript functionality\n├── data/\n│   └── mental-models.json  # Content data\n└── README.md           # This file\n```\n\n## Demo Notes\n\nThis project is designed for live presentation demos. It prioritizes:\n- **Clarity** over cleverness\n- **Simplicity** over complexity\n- **Readability** over optimization\n\nEverything is intentionally straightforward so the audience can understand how it works without frontend expertise.\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
