[2026-01-13 21:44:01] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"272718c0-9cad-4af4-854c-eaaadc4d4243","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"resolve-library-id","tool_input":"{\"libraryName\":\"cursor\",\"query\":\"What are the official Cursor IDE features and documentation URLs?\"}","result_json":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Available Libraries:\\n\\nEach result includes:\\n- Library ID: Context7-compatible identifier (format: /org/project)\\n- Name: Library or package name\\n- Description: Short summary\\n- Code Snippets: Number of available code examples\\n- Source Reputation: Authority indicator (High, Medium, Low, or Unknown)\\n- Benchmark Score: Quality indicator (100 is the highest score)\\n- Versions: List of versions if available. Use one of those versions if the user provides a version in their query. The format of the version is /org/project/version.\\n\\nFor best results, select libraries based on name match, source reputation, snippet coverage, benchmark score, and relevance to your use case.\\n\\n----------\\n\\n- Title: Cursor\\n- Context7-compatible library ID: /getcursor/docs\\n- Description: Cursor is a code editor built for programming with AI, offering features like AI chat, code generation, and debugging.\\n- Code Snippets: 31\\n- Source Reputation: High\\n----------\\n- Title: Cursor\\n- Context7-compatible library ID: /llmstxt/cursor_llms_txt\\n- Description: Cursor is an AI-powered code editor that provides intelligent code completion, agent capabilities, CLI tools, and integration with various development platforms and services.\\n- Code Snippets: 7\\n- Source Reputation: High\\n----------\\n- Title: Cursor CLI\\n- Context7-compatible library ID: /websites/cursor_cli\\n- Description: Cursor CLI allows users to interact with AI agents from the terminal for writing, reviewing, and modifying code, offering both interactive and non-interactive modes for scripting and CI pipelines.\\n- Code Snippets: 101\\n- Source Reputation: High\\n- Benchmark Score: 55.4\\n----------\\n- Title: Cursor (llmstxt)\\n- Context7-compatible library ID: /llmstxt/cursor_llms-full_txt\\n- Description: Cursor provides tools for managing subscriptions, refunds, and invoices, with various pricing plans for individual and team users based on usage and features.\\n- Code Snippets: 5861\\n- Source Reputation: High\\n- Benchmark Score: 60.5\\n----------\\n- Title: Cursor Rules CLI\\n- Context7-compatible library ID: /gabimoncha/cursor-rules-cli\\n- Description: A command-line tool for managing AI-assisted guidance in projects through Cursor IDE rules with interactive setup and security scanning.\\n- Code Snippets: 36\\n- Source Reputation: High\\n- Benchmark Score: 77.6\"}],\"isError\":false}","duration":2235.01,"hook_event_name":"afterMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:44:02] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"272718c0-9cad-4af4-854c-eaaadc4d4243","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"query-docs","tool_input":"{\"libraryId\":\"/getcursor/docs\",\"query\":\"What are the official Cursor IDE feature names like Composer, Chat, and documentation URLs for features like code explanation, teaching, or refactoring?\"}","command":"context7","hook_event_name":"beforeMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:44:11] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"272718c0-9cad-4af4-854c-eaaadc4d4243","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"query-docs","tool_input":"{\"libraryId\":\"/getcursor/docs\",\"query\":\"What are the official Cursor IDE feature names like Composer, Chat, and documentation URLs for features like code explanation, teaching, or refactoring?\"}","result_json":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"### Project-Specific AI Rules\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/rules-for-ai.mdx\\n\\nCreate a `.cursorrules` file in your project's root directory to define custom instructions for AI features. These instructions are specific to the project and are used by features like Cursor Chat and Ctrl/⌘ K.\\n\\n```text\\n.cursorrules\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Apply Code Block\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/apply.mdx\\n\\nIntegrates a code block suggestion from the chat into your current file. This feature allows for quick incorporation of AI-generated code, with changes visible in a diff view.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nApply Code Block:\\n  Description: Integrates a code block suggestion from the chat into your current file.\\n  Action: Click the play button in the top right corner of a chat code block.\\n  Result: Edits the file to incorporate the AI-generated code.\\n  Recommendation: Use for complex AI-driven code changes due to context and back-and-forth capabilities in Chat.\\n\\nAccept/Reject Changes:\\n  Description: Allows users to review and confirm or discard applied code changes.\\n  Accept Shortcut: Ctrl/⌘ Enter\\n  Reject Shortcut: Ctrl/⌘ Backspace\\n  UI Options: 'Accept' or 'Reject' buttons in the top right corner of the chat code block.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Model Management\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/models.mdx\\n\\nThis section details how to interact with and manage AI models within the Cursor IDE. It covers selecting models via a dropdown, adding custom models, and understanding model capabilities like long context support.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nCursor Model Selection:\\n  - Access model selection via Ctrl/⌘ K or the dropdown below the AI input box.\\n  - Default models include: GPT-4o, GPT-4, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, cursor-small.\\n  - 'cursor-small' is a faster, custom model with unlimited access.\\n\\nAdding Custom Models:\\n  - Navigate to `Cursor Settings` > `Models` > `Model Names` to add additional models.\\n\\nLong Context Models:\\n  - Models supporting long context chat include:\\n    - gpt-4o-128k\\n    - gemini-1.5-flash-500k\\n    - claude-3-haiku-200k\\n    - claude-3-sonnet-200k\\n    - claude-3.5-sonnet-200k\\n\\nContext Window Limitations:\\n  - Standard chat: Limited to ~20,000 tokens (or model's max context if less).\\n  - Cmd-K chat: Limited to ~10,000 tokens to balance TTFT and quality.\\n  - Long-context chat: Utilizes the model's maximum context window.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Chat Settings\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/customize.mdx\\n\\nConfiguration options for Cursor Chat, allowing users to tailor its behavior. These settings control aspects like web search integration, visual animations, context handling, and scrolling behavior.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nCursor Settings > Features > Chat:\\n\\n- Always search the web for answers: Enables the AI model to browse the web for up-to-date information with each query.\\n- Add chat fading animation: Applies a smooth animation to AI messages as they are generated.\\n- Default to no context: Configures the AI model to use only the user message as context, excluding additional context like the current file.\\n- Auto scroll chat: Automatically scrolls the chat as the AI generates text when at the bottom of the thread.\\n- Narrow scrollbar in the chat pane: Adjusts the scrollbar width in the chat pane.\\n- Show chat history when starting a new chat: Displays chat history when initiating a new chat session.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Long Context Chat Toggle\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/chat/overview.mdx\\n\\nThis snippet explains how to enable and toggle different modes for the Long Context Chat feature, which allows for larger context windows.\\n\\n```markdown\\nYou can enable long context chat by going to `Cursor Settings` > `Beta` > `Long Context Chat`. With this enabled, you can toggle different chat modes through `Ctrl/⌘ .`.\\n```\"}],\"isError\":false}","duration":9203.426,"hook_event_name":"afterMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:44:13] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"272718c0-9cad-4af4-854c-eaaadc4d4243","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"query-docs","tool_input":"{\"libraryId\":\"/getcursor/docs\",\"query\":\"What are the official Cursor feature names for code explanation, code refactoring, inline suggestions, and what are the official docs.cursor.com documentation URLs?\"}","command":"context7","hook_event_name":"beforeMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:44:16] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"272718c0-9cad-4af4-854c-eaaadc4d4243","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"query-docs","tool_input":"{\"libraryId\":\"/getcursor/docs\",\"query\":\"What are the official Cursor feature names for code explanation, code refactoring, inline suggestions, and what are the official docs.cursor.com documentation URLs?\"}","result_json":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"### Partial Accepts for Suggestions\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/advanced-features.mdx\\n\\nAccept parts of a suggestion, such as the next word, using a keybinding like `Ctrl/⌘` + Right Arrow. This feature requires enabling 'Cursor Tab' in Cursor Settings and allows for more granular control over accepting code suggestions.\\n\\n```editor\\nTo enable partial accepts:\\n1. Navigate to Cursor Settings.\\n2. Go to Features > Cursor Tab.\\n3. Set your preferred keybinding for `editor.action.inlineSuggest.acceptNextWord`.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Tab Interaction\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/overview.mdx\\n\\nExplains how users can interact with code suggestions provided by Cursor Tab. This includes accepting, rejecting, and partially accepting suggestions.\\n\\n```javascript\\n// Accept suggestion by pressing Tab\\n// Reject suggestion by pressing Esc\\n// Partially accept suggestion word-by-word by pressing Ctrl/⌘ →\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Tab Functionality\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/tab/overview.mdx\\n\\nDetails the capabilities of Cursor Tab, including its ability to suggest edits around the cursor, modify multiple lines, and base suggestions on recent changes and linter errors. It also specifies the range of lines it can modify.\\n\\n```cpp\\n// Cursor Tab can suggest edits around your cursor.\\n// It can modify multiple lines at once.\\n// Suggestions are based on recent changes and linter errors.\\n// Cursor can make changes from one line above to two lines below the current line.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Project-Specific AI Rules\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/rules-for-ai.mdx\\n\\nCreate a `.cursorrules` file in your project's root directory to define custom instructions for AI features. These instructions are specific to the project and are used by features like Cursor Chat and Ctrl/⌘ K.\\n\\n```text\\n.cursorrules\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Custom Review Instructions Example\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nProvides an example of custom instructions for the AI Review feature to focus on specific aspects of the code, such as performance.\\n\\n```plaintext\\nfocus on the performance of my code\\n```\"}],\"isError\":false}","duration":3049.907,"hook_event_name":"afterMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 21:44:24] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"272718c0-9cad-4af4-854c-eaaadc4d4243","model":"composer-1","file_path":"/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo/data/mental-models.json","edits":[{"old_string":"","new_string":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-planner\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Planner\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor helps break down complex tasks into manageable steps, creating structured plans before implementation.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor analyzes your request and decomposes it into logical, sequential steps\",\n      \"It identifies dependencies between tasks and suggests an optimal order of execution\",\n      \"The planning phase helps catch potential issues before coding begins\",\n      \"Plans can be reviewed and refined through conversation before implementation\",\n      \"This mental model emphasizes thinking before doing, reducing wasted effort\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Composer\",\n      \"Chat\",\n      \"Multi-file editing\",\n      \"Code generation\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Cursor Documentation\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-pair-programmer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Pair Programmer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor acts as a collaborative coding partner, discussing approaches, reviewing code, and suggesting improvements in real-time.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor engages in back-and-forth dialogue about code design and implementation choices\",\n      \"It provides context-aware suggestions based on your codebase and coding style\",\n      \"Like a human pair programmer, it asks clarifying questions when requirements are ambiguous\",\n      \"It can explain its reasoning and adapt to your feedback during the conversation\",\n      \"This collaborative approach leads to better solutions than one-way code generation\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Chat\",\n      \"Codebase context\",\n      \"Inline suggestions\",\n      \"Code explanations\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Chat Features\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/chat\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-code-reviewer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Code Reviewer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor examines code for bugs, style issues, security vulnerabilities, and opportunities for improvement.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor reviews code with a focus on correctness, maintainability, and best practices\",\n      \"It identifies potential bugs, edge cases, and security concerns before they reach production\",\n      \"The review process considers code style, naming conventions, and architectural patterns\",\n      \"It provides constructive feedback with explanations, not just error messages\",\n      \"This mental model helps maintain code quality and catch issues early in development\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Code analysis\",\n      \"Error detection\",\n      \"Style suggestions\",\n      \"Security scanning\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Code Review\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/review\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-ci-fixer\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a CI Fixer\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor automatically diagnoses and fixes CI/CD pipeline failures, test errors, and build issues.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"When CI fails, Cursor analyzes error messages, logs, and test outputs to identify root causes\",\n      \"It suggests specific fixes for broken tests, compilation errors, and configuration issues\",\n      \"Cursor understands the relationship between code changes and CI failures\",\n      \"It can fix multiple related issues in a single pass, not just one error at a time\",\n      \"This mental model treats CI as a feedback loop that Cursor helps resolve efficiently\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Error analysis\",\n      \"Test fixing\",\n      \"Build debugging\",\n      \"Multi-file changes\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"CI Integration\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/ci\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-knowledge-retriever\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Knowledge Retriever\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor searches through your codebase, documentation, and context to find relevant information and answer questions.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor indexes and understands your entire codebase, making information retrieval fast and accurate\",\n      \"It can answer questions about how code works, where features are implemented, and what patterns are used\",\n      \"The retrieval process considers context, not just keyword matching\",\n      \"It synthesizes information from multiple files and sources to provide comprehensive answers\",\n      \"This mental model positions Cursor as a searchable knowledge base of your project\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Codebase indexing\",\n      \"Semantic search\",\n      \"Context awareness\",\n      \"Documentation lookup\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Codebase Context\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/context\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cursor-as-teacher\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor as a Teacher\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Cursor explains code concepts, teaches best practices, and helps developers understand how things work and why they matter.\",\n    \"detailedExplanation\": [\n      \"Cursor breaks down complex code into understandable concepts, explaining not just what code does but why it's written that way\",\n      \"It teaches programming patterns, design principles, and best practices through contextual explanations\",\n      \"When you ask 'how does this work?' or 'why is this better?', Cursor provides educational answers that deepen understanding\",\n      \"It adapts explanations to your skill level, providing beginner-friendly introductions or advanced deep-dives as needed\",\n      \"This mental model positions Cursor as a patient tutor that helps you grow as a developer through continuous learning\"\n    ],\n    \"relatedFeatures\": [\n      \"Chat\",\n      \"Code explanations\",\n      \"Codebase context\",\n      \"Inline suggestions\",\n      \"Documentation lookup\"\n    ],\n    \"docs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Chat Features\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/chat\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Codebase Context\",\n        \"url\": \"https://docs.cursor.com/context\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n"}],"hook_event_name":"afterFileEdit","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
