[2026-01-13 22:04:46] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"90358a85-9b0b-4fa0-8250-0ab5ade04bac","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"query-docs","tool_input":"{\"libraryId\":\"/getcursor/docs\",\"query\":\"What is this repository about? Answer in two sentences.\"}","command":"context7","hook_event_name":"beforeMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
[2026-01-13 22:04:48] {"conversation_id":"85a0d59b-abeb-4a4b-b83e-d02ce54c77f0","generation_id":"90358a85-9b0b-4fa0-8250-0ab5ade04bac","model":"composer-1","tool_name":"query-docs","tool_input":"{\"libraryId\":\"/getcursor/docs\",\"query\":\"What is this repository about? Answer in two sentences.\"}","result_json":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"### Review Options\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nLists the available options for initiating an AI Review, specifying which set of code changes to analyze.\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Working State\\n# This will review your uncommitted changes.\\n```\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Diff with Main Branch\\n# This will review the diff between your current working state and the main branch.\\n```\\n\\n```shell\\n# Review Last Commit\\n# This will review the last commit you made.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Custom Review Instructions Example\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/ai-review.mdx\\n\\nProvides an example of custom instructions for the AI Review feature to focus on specific aspects of the code, such as performance.\\n\\n```plaintext\\nfocus on the performance of my code\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cmd K Chunking Strategies\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/@-symbols/@-files.mdx\\n\\nDescribes the different strategies Cursor uses for chunking files in Cmd K based on file size and content.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nCmd K Chunking Strategies:\\n\\n- auto: Automatically picks one of three reading strategies based on file size.\\n- full file: Uses the entire file as context.\\n- outline: Parses the file's outline and uses that information as context.\\n- chunks: Chunks the file into smaller pieces and selects the most relevant chunk.\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Project-Specific AI Rules\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/context/rules-for-ai.mdx\\n\\nCreate a `.cursorrules` file in your project's root directory to define custom instructions for AI features. These instructions are specific to the project and are used by features like Cursor Chat and Ctrl/⌘ K.\\n\\n```text\\n.cursorrules\\n```\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\n### Cursor Model Management\\n\\nSource: https://github.com/getcursor/docs/blob/main/advanced/models.mdx\\n\\nThis section details how to interact with and manage AI models within the Cursor IDE. It covers selecting models via a dropdown, adding custom models, and understanding model capabilities like long context support.\\n\\n```APIDOC\\nCursor Model Selection:\\n  - Access model selection via Ctrl/⌘ K or the dropdown below the AI input box.\\n  - Default models include: GPT-4o, GPT-4, Claude 3.5 Sonnet, cursor-small.\\n  - 'cursor-small' is a faster, custom model with unlimited access.\\n\\nAdding Custom Models:\\n  - Navigate to `Cursor Settings` > `Models` > `Model Names` to add additional models.\\n\\nLong Context Models:\\n  - Models supporting long context chat include:\\n    - gpt-4o-128k\\n    - gemini-1.5-flash-500k\\n    - claude-3-haiku-200k\\n    - claude-3-sonnet-200k\\n    - claude-3.5-sonnet-200k\\n\\nContext Window Limitations:\\n  - Standard chat: Limited to ~20,000 tokens (or model's max context if less).\\n  - Cmd-K chat: Limited to ~10,000 tokens to balance TTFT and quality.\\n  - Long-context chat: Utilizes the model's maximum context window.\\n```\"}],\"isError\":false}","duration":2419.096,"hook_event_name":"afterMCPExecution","cursor_version":"2.3.15","workspace_roots":["/Users/tamar/cursor-mental-models-demo"],"user_email":"t0548453823@gmail.com"}
